{
  "summary": "A day trip in Shibuya with minimal Japanese knowledge can still be thoroughly enjoyable and easy to navigate. Start your day at the iconic Shibuya Crossing, followed by a visit to the Hachiko Statue. Explore the trendy shops and cafes in the area, and enjoy a meal at a conveyor belt sushi restaurant, which requires minimal interaction. Spend the afternoon at Yoyogi Park and visit the nearby Meiji Shrine. End your day with a panoramic view of the city from the Shibuya Sky observation deck.",
  "tips": [
    "Use translation apps or carry a phrasebook to help with basic interactions.",
    "Look for restaurants with picture menus or English menus, which are common in tourist areas.",
    "Stay close to major landmarks and use the English signage available in most public transport and popular tourist spots."
